# {{projectNameHuman}}

Scaffolded with `forge` from the `fullstack-spring-react` template.

- `backend/` — Spring Boot (Maven), package `{{mainPackage}}`, serves the API on `:8080`
- `frontend/` — Vite + React + TypeScript, dev server on `:5173` (proxies `/api` to the backend)

## Run it

```bash
npm install       # installs the root dev-orchestration package (concurrently)
npm run dev        # runs backend + frontend together
```

Or run each side on its own:

```bash
cd backend && mvn spring-boot:run
cd frontend && npm install && npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173. The landing page calls `GET /api/hello` through the
proxy and shows the result, so you can see straight away whether both halves are
talking to each other. If the backend is not running, the page says so instead of
failing silently.

{{#if addons}}
## Frontend add-ons

Picked at scaffold time, so this copy only has what you selected:

{{/if}}
{{#if framerMotion}}
- **Framer Motion** — one animated card in `frontend/src/App.tsx` as a working example.
{{/if}}
{{#if lucideReact}}
- **Lucide React** — icons imported per component.
{{/if}}
{{#if tailwind}}
- **Tailwind CSS** — wired through `@tailwindcss/vite`, no config file needed to start.
{{/if}}
{{#if rtkQuery}}
- **RTK Query** — `frontend/src/store/` holds the store and an API slice pointed at
  this project's own backend, so the call on the landing page goes through RTK Query
  rather than plain `fetch`.
{{/if}}

## Build

```bash
npm run build
```

Builds the frontend to `frontend/dist/` and packages the backend jar in `backend/target/`.
